le-mounted. The Pak 40 was very effective against almost every Allied tank, and could fire up to 14 rounds per minute, but it had some problems with penetrating some of the Allied late war heavy tanks.","LocalizedString":"The 7.5 cm Pak 40 was German anti-tank gun that was used by the Wehrmacht and their allies during WWII. The gun was produced from 1942 to 1945, with 23,303 units built, and it became the main German anti-tank gun for the latter part of WWII. It was mostly towed or used on a number of tank destroyers, but a variant was made that could be vehicle-mounted. The Pak 40 was very effective against almost every Allied tank, and could fire up to 14 rounds per minute, but it had some problems with penetrating some of the Allied late war heavy tanks."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Ambush","EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment"],"hasDeployment":true,"hasAmbush":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Artillery_Move_FX'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Artillery_Move_FX.0"},"soundMoveToFrontline":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Artillery_Move_FX'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Artillery_Move_FX.0"},"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Medium'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Medium.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/CandidateArtwork/WE_Candidates/t_pak_40.t_pak_40","SubPathString":""},"artist":"David Pentland","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/PAK_40.PAK_40","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":352.0},"historyPhotoSource":"German Federal Archives","historyPhotoIdentificationCode":"101I-296-1688-30A","historyPhotoAuthor":"Schwoon","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_pak_40_photo","SourceString":"A 